## Bank rejected claim payments due to routing number format; integration adapter updated to zero-pad.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-400003)
**Module:** ClaimCenter | **Category:** IntegrationFailure | **Severity:** SEV1-Critical
**Resolution Type:** CodeFix
**Date:** 2025-11-07
**Guidewire Version:** Jasper

### Summary / Symptom
Claim payments to vendors are being rejected by the bank integration. The error message from the bank API says the routing number format is invalid. This started after the bank updated their API to require a 9-digit zero-padded format. Approximately 85 vendor payments are stuck in pending state.

### Resolution
The root cause was the payment integration adapter sending 8-digit routing numbers, while the bank's updated API required a 9-digit zero-padded format. The integration code was updated to always zero-pad routing numbers to 9 digits before sending. After this fix, the 85 previously stuck vendor payments were reprocessed and successfully accepted by the bank. This resolved the integration failure and restored normal payment processing.


