## Adjuster notes failed to save with >50 attachments; fixed file handle leak and config limit.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-500001)
**Module:** ClaimCenter | **Category:** PerformanceDegradation | **Severity:** SEV1-Critical
**Resolution Type:** CodeFix
**Date:** 2025-11-12
**Guidewire Version:** Innsbruck

### Summary / Symptom
Adjuster notes are failing to save when claims have more than 50 attachments. Adjusters can work around this by splitting notes into smaller entries or removing older attachments temporarily. The issue is intermittent and affects roughly 20 active large-loss claims.

### Resolution
The root cause was a file descriptor limit in the attachment service, triggered when claims had more than 50 attachments. The service was not releasing file handles after previewing attachments, leading to intermittent failures when saving adjuster notes. The issue was resolved by explicitly cleaning up file handles in the attachment service code and increasing the per-process file descriptor limit in the server configuration. After these changes, all affected claims were verified as able to save notes without issue.


