## Fleet discount tier misapplied in commercial auto rating; Gosu rule index corrected and redeployed.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-500002)
**Module:** PolicyCenter | **Category:** ConfigurationError | **Severity:** SEV2-High
**Resolution Type:** CodeFix
**Date:** 2025-11-14
**Guidewire Version:** Jasper

### Summary / Symptom
Premium rating for commercial auto policies is producing results that differ from the manual rate calculation sheet by 3-8%. The difference appears only on policies with more than 5 vehicles. Underwriters are manually checking and correcting premiums before binding.

### Resolution
The root cause was a Gosu rule in PolicyCenter's commercial auto rating logic that incorrectly applied a fleet discount tier using a 0-indexed lookup instead of 1-indexed, resulting in the wrong discount for policies with more than five vehicles. The issue was resolved by correcting the index offset in the Gosu rule and redeploying the fix. Additionally, endorsements were initiated to remediate premiums on 14 affected bound policies. This ensured both future and past policies were corrected.


